(window.DVR_PAPERS=window.DVR_PAPERS||{})["ce-easy-2026-007"]={"v":1,"id":"ce-easy-2026-007","title":"Basic Level Test-3 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 CE","sourceTitle":"Basic Level Test-3 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 CE","branch":"CIVIL ENGINEERING","code":"CE","provider":"DVRUO EASY","providerKey":"easy","series":"GATE 2026 + ESE 2026 Online Test Series - Civil Engineering","seriesId":"ce-easy-2026","num":7,"category":"basic","year":"2026","format":"A","durationSec":10800,"info":{"meta":"Package: GATE 2026 + ESE 2026 Online Test Series - Civil Engineering • Questions: 65","package":"GATE 2026 + ESE 2026 Online Test Series - Civil Engineering"},"source":"CIVIL ENGINEERING/MADE EASY/GATE 2026 + ESE 2026 Online Test Series - Civil Engineering/007_Basic Level Test-3 Full Syllabus GATE 2026 CE.html","questions":[{"n":1,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>If the number 18601<em>x</em>57y is divisible by 72, then <em>x</em> + y =</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"7"},{"key":"B","html":"8"},{"key":"C","html":"9"},{"key":"D","html":"6"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/80/80dd841e1d6e77455230.png\" /></div>"},{"n":2,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A page contains 60 lines. A chapter contains 125 pages. A book contains 5 chapters. 20 such books form a bound. If there are total 30 lakh lines in an <em>x</em> number of bounds, then the value of <em>x</em> is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"4"},{"key":"B","html":"2"},{"key":"C","html":"5"},{"key":"D","html":"6"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/89/898f8a90bed578fb9b44.png\" /></div>"},{"n":3,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A circular paper is folded along its diameter, then again it is folded to form a quadrant. Then it is cut as shown in the figure and after that the paper was reopened in the original circular shape. What is the ratio of area of the original paper to that of the remaining paper? (The shaded portion is cut off from the quadrant. The radius of quadrant OAB is 5 cm and radius of each semicircle is 1 cm).</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/91/916d585fc2d0eeec9c6f.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"25 : 16"},{"key":"B","html":"25 : 9"},{"key":"C","html":"20 : 9"},{"key":"D","html":"None of these"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/78/786a5b18e0d3a8eb1128.png\" /></div>"},{"n":4,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A number when divided successively by 4, 5, 6 leaves remainder 2, 3 and 5 respectively. What is the minimum such number?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"214"},{"key":"B","html":"224"},{"key":"C","html":"114"},{"key":"D","html":"354"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d7/d7796bad057c6dab4a42.png\" /></div>"},{"n":5,"type":"NAT","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A is thrice as efficient as <em>B</em>. Working together they complete the work in 3 days. If <em>B</em> takes 8 days more than <em>A</em>, the number of days taken by <em>A</em> to finish the whole work, alone is _______ days.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[4,4],"answerText":"4","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>4 (4 - 4)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/2a/2a88f4da97a34a6de2c9.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":6,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In the following question, four alternatives are given for the bold word. Choose the word which is most similar in meaning (Synonym).<br />\n<strong>Previously</strong></p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Rested"},{"key":"B","html":"Limited"},{"key":"C","html":"Formerly"},{"key":"D","html":"Mindless"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)<br />\nThe word &ldquo;previously&rdquo; means earlier or before now. Its closest synonym is &ldquo;formerly.&rdquo;</p>"},{"n":7,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Read the passage carefully and answer the following question.<br />\nAmong Nature’s most intriguing phenomena are the partnerships formed by many different species. The name used for these relationships, Symbiosis, comes from Greek meaning “living together”. Not all symbiotic relationships are the same. There are some called commensal relationships, in which one partner gains a benefit while the other gains little or none but is not<br />\nharmed. One example is the relationship between two types of fish – remoras and sharks. The remora, which is long and often striped, attaches itself to a shark (sometimes to another type of fish or a whale), using a sucker on its head. When the shark makes a kill, the hitchhiker briefly detaches itself to feed on the scraps. Another type of symbiotic relationship is parasitism, in which one partner benefits at the expense of others. Ticks and tapeworms are among familiar parasites.<br />\nThe third type of symbiotic relationship, called mutualism, is a true partnership in which both partners benefit. The relationship may be limited as when zebras and wildebeest graze together on the vast African grasslands. Each species can survive on its own, but together their chances of detecting predators are improved because each contributes a specially keen sense. (Zebras have<br />\nthe better eyesight; wildebeest, hearing and sense of smell). In a few cases, partners are so interdependent that one cannot survive without the other. Most mutualistic relationships probably lie somewhere in between.<br />\nThe passage talks about how animals</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"attack/prey each other"},{"key":"B","html":"live together mutual dependance"},{"key":"C","html":"take advantage of the weaker ones"},{"key":"D","html":"are independent of each other"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nThe passage talks about symbiosis i.e. how animals live together.</p>"},{"n":8,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A started a business with <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/40/407a07c0ef37fa34bd6e.png\" /> and after 4 months <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/31/3105057612fcfe521879.png\" /> joined him with <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/ec/eca1b923ca416d58d2aa.png\" /> At the end of the year, out of the total profits <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/19/1958750e6f1122c4ca01.png\" /> received total <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/21/21da89de0d53871c0cc2.png\" /> including 25% of the profits as commission for managing the business. What amount did <em>A</em> receive?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/95/9563a855f2622b2561e8.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0e/0ef8c4908d2a174bc331.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/48/48e41aaf3ec11f65d50f.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c6/c6884350447ef8ccf81c.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ec/eca5b6fb4c1cb284a12d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":9,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Kailash faces towards north. Turning to his right, he walks 25 metres. He then turns to his left and walks 30 metres. Next, he moves 25 metres to his right. He then turns to his right again and walks 55 metres. Finally, he turns to the right and moves 40 metres. In which direction is he now from his starting point?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"South-west"},{"key":"B","html":"South"},{"key":"C","html":"North-west"},{"key":"D","html":"South-east"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/98/989e002017015899f421.png\" /></div>"},{"n":10,"type":"MCQ","section":"General Aptitude","tags":"General Aptitude • ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>For the mirror represented by a line MN, choose the correct mirror-image of the figure, from amongst the four alternatives (a), (b), (c) and (d) given along with it.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4d/4d4cd6b0914613c53e1c.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d5/d599f5d8be136dec0d3d.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/88/88b46ddc2495d247d9cc.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/65/650aeb2bc5d572322997.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ab/abd9b135231b6fd56a92.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>"},{"n":11,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>For a solid circular shaft subjected to torsion, which one of the following statements is true about the shear stress distribution?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Shear stress is uniform across the cross-section."},{"key":"B","html":"Shear stress is zero at the outer surface and maximum at the center."},{"key":"C","html":"Shear stress varies linearly from zero at the center to maximum at the outer surface."},{"key":"D","html":"Shear stress varies parabolically with the maximum at the center."}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>"},{"n":12,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A closed traverse <em>ABCDA</em> was run and the observed data for its sides are provided in the table below. It is required to connect point <em>E</em>, the midpoint of side <em>BC</em>, with point <em>F</em>, the midpoint of side <em>AD</em>.</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/84/8459392e6692b4ed5f6b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The bearing of line <em>EF</em> is:</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<em>N</em>73°07'<em>E</em>"},{"key":"B","html":"<em>S</em>71°18'<em>W</em>"},{"key":"C","html":"S73°07'<em>W</em>"},{"key":"D","html":"<em>N</em>71°18'<em>E</em>"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d5/d5d5cc8366e22eb3ead7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9d/9da29277e8e59b17a98f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":13,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Consider the following statements:<br />\n1. If a three hinged parabolic arch is subjected to a uniformly distributed load, the moment at any section in the arch is zero.<br />\n2. If a three hinged arch is initially loaded and temperature is increased, then horizontal reaction decreases and vertical reaction increases.</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Statement 1 is true, 2 is false"},{"key":"B","html":"Both the statements are true"},{"key":"C","html":"Statement 1 is false, 2 is true"},{"key":"D","html":"Both the statements are false"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)<br />\nStatement 1 is true because the structure is funicular with respect to the loading i.e., the shape of<br />\nthe bending moment as well as the structure&rsquo;s geometry is similar in proportion, therefore, the<br />\nbending moment will be zero.<br />\nStatement 2 is false<br />\nIf the three hinged arch is initially loaded and temperature is increased, then horizontal reaction<br />\ndecreases and vertical reaction remains unaffected.</p>"},{"n":14,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The following table provides the areas of strips between successive isohyets for a catchment basin. According to this data, the average precipitation over the basin is:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/b1/b14777f9ac458a8a1b8a.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"126.1 cm"},{"key":"B","html":"111.6 cm"},{"key":"C","html":"97.1 cm"},{"key":"D","html":"88.4 cm"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/40/405326fc8eb15059c338.png\" /></div>"},{"n":15,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A manometer consists of a uniform glass tube having a cross-sectional area of 0.6 cm<sup>2</sup>. One limb of the tube is vertical, while the other is inclined at 40° to the horizontal. Both limbs are open to the atmosphere and the tube initially contains a manometric fluid of specific gravity 1.20. If an additional 8 cm<sup>3</sup> of water is carefully poured into the inclined limb, the rise of the meniscus in the vertical limb is ______ cm. (Answer upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[4.1,4.7],"answerText":"4.35","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>4.35 (4.10 - 4.70)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/1b/1b6b92e7942b6e018f54.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d2/d27e7527ea17c96cd10e.png\" /></div>"},{"n":16,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A simply supported beam <em>AB</em> is subjected to a distributed load of intensity <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/e2/e219182c35fc4b6d93e9.png\" /> as shown in figure. If the magnitude of deflection at the mid span of the beam is <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/4c/4ca63daa66802b4977a7.png\" /> then the value of α is ______ (Correct upto two decimal places).</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/48/488608da6162e89d0a60.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[97,98],"answerText":"97.4","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>97.4 (97 - 98)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/80/8061835bc3ddff360f08.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ef/ef981424b6a3d15acd18.png\" /></div>"},{"n":17,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Which of the following statements are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"An ascending gradient of 1 in 100 meets an ascending gradient of 1 in 120 to form valley curve."},{"key":"B","html":"An ascending gradient of 1 in 100 meets an ascending gradient of 1 in 120 to form summit curve."},{"key":"C","html":"A falling gradient of 1 in 80 meets an ascending gradient of 1 in 50 to form valley curve."},{"key":"D","html":"A falling gradient of 1 in 80 meets a falling gradient of 1 in 50 to form valley curve."}],"answer":["B","C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B, C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(b , c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cd/cd05674ad7e5ba157520.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":18,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A circular footing is proposed for a building foundation on a cohesive soil stratum. The footing has a diameter of 2.5 m and is placed at a depth of 1.5 m below the ground surface. The soil investigation reports the following properties: cohesion of 50 kN/m2, total unit weight of 19.5 kN/m<sup>3</sup>, saturated unit weight of 21 kN/m<sup>3</sup> and angle of internal friction as 0°. The groundwater table is observed at a depth of 0.7 m below the ground level. If a factor of safety of 3.0 is used for design against shear failure, the safe load carrying capacity of the footing using Terzaghi’s theory is :</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"715.8 kN"},{"key":"B","html":"681 kN"},{"key":"C","html":"642.7 kN"},{"key":"D","html":"687.5 kN"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/54/54f49058630c7a27caa7.png\" /></div>"},{"n":19,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A circular sewer is laid on a slope of 1 in 450 to serve a population of 52000. The per capita water supply is 140 l/day and 80% of this gets converted into sewage. Assume a peaking factor of 3.2 for maximum discharge. The sewer runs 0.7 times full at the time of maximum flow. If the Manning’s roughness coefficient is 0.012, then the diameter of sewer will be ________ m. (Answer upto three decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.5,0.6],"answerText":"0.558","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.558 (0.5 - 0.60)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d6/d6819b2721cc48ba65cc.png\" /></div>"},{"n":20,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>What is the average skid resistance for a vehicle which is running at a speed of 60 kmph and stopped in 2.25 sec after the application of brakes ______ (correct upto two decimal places)?<br />\n[Take, g = 10 m/s<sup>2</sup>].</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.72,0.76],"answerText":"0.74","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.74 (0.72 - 0.76)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f1/f176c0be50bf89c8edc5.png\" /></div>"},{"n":21,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>Let <em>B</em> is an invertible square matrix and B is the adjoint of matrix A such that <em>AB</em> = <em>B<sup>T</sup></em>. Then which of the following options is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<em>A</em> is an identity matrix"},{"key":"B","html":"<em>B</em> is a symmetric matrix"},{"key":"C","html":"<em>A</em> is a skew-symmetric matrix"},{"key":"D","html":"<em>B</em> is a skew-symmetric matrix"}],"answer":["A","B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/50/509c376265d7b2cce6af.png\" /></div>\n</div>"},{"n":22,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A hat contains a number of cards, with 30% white on both sides, 50% black on one side and white on the other side, 20% black on both sides. The cards are mixed up, and a single card is drawn at random and placed on the table. If It’s upper side shows up black, the probability that its other side is also black is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4c/4c662619a509078acc50.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/79/795c8c4a98ddb22f9cf8.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9d/9dffe5bf3370909d8cbd.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f8/f8e18cc1ba9b8f7680c5.png\" />"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cc/cca166f4d5bd6a125bfc.png\" /></div>"},{"n":23,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>In a horizontal rectangular channel, a hydraulic jump occurs resulting in the post-jump velocity and depth of flow being 0.95 m/s and 1.8 m respectively. The correct statement(s) corresponding to this hydraulic jump is/are:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Depth before the jump = 0.168 m"},{"key":"B","html":"Energy loss = 3.594 m"},{"key":"C","html":"Power dissipated per meter width = 56.73 kW"},{"key":"D","html":"Power dissipated per meter width = 60.29 kW"}],"answer":["A","B","D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B, D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b, d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d1/d1dc692e7d5d3d5f9c7c.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9b/9b0fa2175824f6b8cfa0.png\" /></div>"},{"n":24,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>Which one of the following statements regarding slow sand filters and rapid sand filters is incorrect?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Rapid sand filters operate at much higher filtration rates and are cleaned by backwashing."},{"key":"B","html":"Slow sand filters do not function well with highly turbid water."},{"key":"C","html":"Slow sand filters utilise coarser sand than rapid sand filters."},{"key":"D","html":"Rapid sand filters have a larger rate of filtration than slow sand filters."}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>"},{"n":25,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A reinforced concrete column of 4.5 m upsupported length and size 600 mm × 600 mm is designed to carry a load of 3000 kN. The column is made of M25 concrete and reinforced with 20 mm diameter bars of Fe415 steel. The area of steel required for longitudinal reinforcement is:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"2285 mm<sup>2</sup>"},{"key":"B","html":"3285 mm<sup>2</sup>"},{"key":"C","html":"3358 mm<sup>2</sup>"},{"key":"D","html":"4258 mm<sup>2</sup>"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7a/7a884aed804ea546dc2a.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/df/df760a8df6eda652a3a2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":26,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>For the flow setup shown in the figure, the hydraulic conductivities of the two soil samples, soil 1 and soil 2, are 10 mm/s and 20 mm/s respectively. Assume that the unit weight of water is 10 kN/m<sup>3</sup>. The value of effective stress at point <em>A</em> is ________ kPa.<br />\nAssume: Tail water level as datum and γ<sub>sat</sub> = 20 kN/m<sup>3</sup></p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f4/f47469ccbad962a265e8.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"60"},{"key":"B","html":"50"},{"key":"C","html":"70"},{"key":"D","html":"40"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/68/686b4ee5ffa4113761e8.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fe/fe467fd1dbd65b8b3e60.png\" /></div>"},{"n":27,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A wide rectangular channel conveys a discharge of 3.2 m3/s per meter width under a uniform flow depth of 1.8 m. The corresponding fall in the water surface level when the channel bed is raised by the minimum amount necessary to achieve critical flow at that section is ____ m. (Answer upto three decimal places) [Take <em>g</em> = 9.81 m/s<sup>2</sup>]</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[0.33,0.37],"answerText":"0.346","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>0.346 (0.330 - 0.370)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/74/74ee79ade00e9ea9e78f.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":28,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>Consider the truss shown below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5b/5b8629ad7fd9927b753d.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>The number of zero force member(s) is ______</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[8,8],"answerText":"8","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>8 (8 - 8)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/80/80308e277110a7add0dc.png\" /></div>"},{"n":29,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Which of the following statements is not true about high alumina cement?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"It is not a type of Portland cement."},{"key":"B","html":"It has poor sulphate resistance."},{"key":"C","html":"It has high heat of hydration"},{"key":"D","html":"It does not set quickly."}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nIn high alumina cement, <em>C</em><sub>3</sub><em>A</em> is not present. Hence, the cement has good sulphate resistance.</p>"},{"n":30,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A wastewater sample was diluted to 8% with aerated tap water for conducting a BOD test. The<br />\ndissolved oxygen of the dilution water was 7.2 <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/97/97b388f31a984b320e7a.png\" /> and that of wastewater was 1.6 <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/97/97b388f31a984b320e7a.png\" />. After<br />\n5 days of incubation at 20°C, the dissolved oxygen of the diluted sample was found to be 3.8 <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/97/97b388f31a984b320e7a.png\" />. Assuming the reaction rate constant, <em>K</em><sub>20</sub> = 0.10 per day (base 10), the ultimate BOD of the waste water is:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e0/e015010a22e154e03562.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/33/3377355e4261965f518b.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0f/0f559fba3236da567536.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ef/ef0778e1911b8ea457b3.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c2/c29f0ae77b2a54c949b8.png\" /></div>"},{"n":31,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A 6 m thick clay layer is located between two layers of free draining sand. A thin drainage layer is embedded within the clay at a depth of 1.5 m from its top surface. The degree of consolidation (%<em>U</em>) in the upper and lower portions of the clay layer (split by the internal drain) is found to be in the ratio of 3 : 1 at any given time while the ratio of their ultimate settlements is 1 : 3 respectively.<br />\nIf a structure is constructed over the clay layer, the time required for the clay layer to attain 50% of its ultimate settlement is _____ days. (Answer upto two decimal places).<br />\nTake coefficient of consolidation as 4.92 × 10<sup>–4</sup> cm<sup>2</sup>/sec.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[103.5,104.5],"answerText":"103.93","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>103.93 (103.5 - 104.5)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d3/d394a50706271e222b10.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":32,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The modulus of elasticity of the pavement material (E<sub>1</sub>) is 120 MN/m<sup>2</sup> and that of subgrade (<em>E</em><sub>2</sub>) is 12 MN/m<sup>2</sup>. The thickness of a flexible pavement as per Burmister's two layer theory for a wheel load of 40 kN, tyre pressure of 0.5 MN/m<sup>2</sup> and an allowable deflection of 0.5 cm is ____ cm. The value of deflection factor for <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/19/191468d6f4a619847109.png\" /> of 10 can be taken as below:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/64/64aeef02e573166714f7.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>where is a radius of contact area.</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"12 cm"},{"key":"B","html":"14 cm"},{"key":"C","html":"16 cm"},{"key":"D","html":"18 cm"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/29/292002b9fb2cf036bf76.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":33,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A 400 g dry soil sample was subjected to sieve analysis, and the following data were obtained:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/97/9752da7f72565c3544c8.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>For this grain size distribution, which of the following statements is/are CORRECT?</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Uniformity coefficient of the soil is 0.833."},{"key":"B","html":"Coefficient of curvature of the soil is 3.33."},{"key":"C","html":"The soil can be classified as well graded."},{"key":"D","html":"The soil can be classified as gap graded."}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/34/34855919e1150d367796.png\" /></div>"},{"n":34,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A rectangular channel 3 m wide conveys water at a uniform depth of 1.5 m. The bed slope of the channel is 0.0025. Assuming steady uniform flow and the specific weight of water as 9.81 kN/m<sup>3</sup>, the average shear stress acting on the channel bed is _____ <em>Pa</em>. (Answer upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[18.15,18.65],"answerText":"18.39","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>18.39 (18.15 - 18.65)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d5/d57f725cb98d1c946005.png\" /></div>"},{"n":35,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The value of <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/49/49cd5d86435a98e8281b.png\" /> where ‘c’ is the closed curve of the region bounded by <em>y</em> = <em>x</em><sup>2</sup> and <em>y</em><sup>2</sup> = <em>x</em> is ________.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[-0.8,-0.4],"answerText":"-0.6","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>-0.6 (-0.8 - -0.4)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/9c/9c96b98e43b0287d2331.png\" /></div>"},{"n":36,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A moist sample of soil (<em>G</em> = 2.7) was tested using a pycnometer for determination of water content.<br />\nThe following observations were made:<br />\n• Mass of empty pycnometer = 600 gm<br />\n• Mass of pycnometer + moist soil = 1050 gm<br />\n• Mass of pycnometer + soil sample + water (filled to the top) = 1850 gm<br />\n• Mass of pycnometer + water = 1650 gm<br />\nThe water content of soil sample is:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"13.33%"},{"key":"B","html":"41.67%"},{"key":"C","html":"18%"},{"key":"D","html":"25.73%"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/54/54cf661fa9a7708e4e2f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":37,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>In an incompressible flow, the velocity vector is given by</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/65/655c0f681c8ae97336ba.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The magnitude of the acceleration vector at point <em>P</em>(2, 1, 0) at <em>t</em> = 1 is ______ . (Answer upto two decimal points)</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[90,92],"answerText":"91","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>91 (90 - 92)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/5e/5e06853ca44fe631329c.png\" /></div>"},{"n":38,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A vertical retaining wall of height 12 m retains a horizontal backfill of cohesionless soil with an angle of internal friction of 35°. The backfill consists of two layers with top 4 m having a unit weight of 18 kN/m<sup>3</sup> and the remaining lower layer having a unit weight of 24 kN/m<sup>3</sup>. The total horizontal active thrust on the wall per meter length is ____ kN/m. (Answer upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[403,403.5],"answerText":"403.25","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>403.25 (403 - 403.5)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/54/540a22bb058e95ee2850.png\" /></div>"},{"n":39,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>A simply supported pre-stressed concrete beam of span 25 m is initially prestressed with 1000 N/mm<sup>2</sup>. During tensioning phase there occurs a slip in jack of 5 mm. If the elastic modulus of prestressing wire is 205 GPa, then the loss in prestress due to slip will be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"5.1%"},{"key":"B","html":"4.1%"},{"key":"C","html":"5.9%"},{"key":"D","html":"4.9%"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/49/498bdb2ba5f1fee6cc6f.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":40,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A rainfall event of constant intensity and duration uniformly covers a watershed with welldefined boundaries. The resulting direct run-off hydrograph shows a pronounced peak shortly after rainfall ends and then rapidly declines. Which combination of watershed characteristics most likely produced this hydrograph shape?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"Large area, low slope, dense forest cover, clayey soil"},{"key":"B","html":"Small area, steep slope, urbanized surface, clayey soil"},{"key":"C","html":"Large area, high slope, agricultural land, sandy soil"},{"key":"D","html":"Small area, low slope, grassland cover, gravelly soil"}],"answer":["B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nA small catchment with steep slopes, urbanised impervious surfaces and clayey soils will<br />\nconcentrate runoff quickly, resulting in a sharp peak and rapid recession of the direct runoff<br />\nhydrograph.</p>"},{"n":41,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>An area measuring 24 km × 18 km is to be covered by vertical aerial photographs, each having a size of 230 mm × 230 mm. The photographic scale is such that 1 cm on the photograph represents 200 m on the ground. If the longitudinal overlap is 55% and the side overlap is 25%, then the total number of photographs required to cover the entire area is _____. (Answer in integer value).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[90,92],"answerText":"91","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>91 (90 - 92)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/84/8434c279907fa349164d.png\" /></div>"},{"n":42,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>An open well is to yield a steady discharge of 4.5 l/s under a depression head of 2.5 m. The specific yield of the aquifer is 1.2 m<sup>3</sup>/hr per m<sup>2 </sup>of well area. The corresponding diameter of the well is ______ m. (Answer upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[2.4,2.8],"answerText":"2.62","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>2.62 (2.40 - 2.80)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/18/18d410a93454531f1d0a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":43,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A maintenance project’s duration is to be crashed by 3 days. If the overhead costs are Rs. 3000 per day then, the total project cost after crashing will be Rs. _____. (Round off to nearest integer).</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/93/936051b083d9bd135aa1.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[65000,65000],"answerText":"65000","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>65000&nbsp; (65000 - 65000)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/92/92b4d38b8c1904b646c0.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":44,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A simply supported beam of span 10 m and having circular cross-section is loaded with a uniformly distributed load over the entire span. The plastic hinge length at the time of collapse will be _____ m. (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[6.4,6.5],"answerText":"6.42","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>6.42 (6.4 - 6.5)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e6/e61d88c6526265fe68f6.png\" /></div>"},{"n":45,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A high rate trickling filter is to treat 4.5 MLD of waste water having an influent BOD of 150 <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/cf/cf77fb2c61a6002fdff0.png\" /><br />\nThe primary clarifier removes 30% of the BOD before the filter. The required effluent BOD is 20 <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/ef/ef9d36c055378a2e146e.png\" /> The recirculation ratio is 1.4 and the depth of the filter is 1.6 m. The required volume of the filter tank will be:</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"892.85 m<sup>3</sup>"},{"key":"B","html":"1275.5 m<sup>3</sup>"},{"key":"C","html":"382.65 m<sup>3</sup>"},{"key":"D","html":"586.32 m<sup>3</sup>"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ac/ac75988d62e9db9d992b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f5/f5baf76695b1bbcad0a8.png\" /></div>"},{"n":46,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>For a given system of two blocks as shown in the figure, the maximum value of force '<em>F</em>' (in N, correct up to nearest integer) for which both the blocks will move together is _____ .<br />\n(Take <em>g</em> = 10 m/s<sup>2</sup>)</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ae/ae5fa106b182db6e8cda.png\" /></div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[31,33],"answerText":"32","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>32 (31 - 33)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4f/4f418263edd772ba5364.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/dc/dce4eaeb966253003758.png\" /></div>"},{"n":47,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>Consider the function <em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) given as:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3a/3aaf95d1bb0eb0413a8f.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>Which of the below statements is correct?</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) is continuous at <em>x</em> = 2"},{"key":"B","html":"<em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) has removable discontinuity at <em>x</em> = 2"},{"key":"C","html":"<em>f</em> (<em>x</em>) has non-removable discontinuity at <em>x</em> = 2"},{"key":"D","html":"Discontinuity at <em>x</em> = 2 can be removed by redefining the function at <em>x</em> = 2"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4a/4ace1a64202635f124d6.png\" /></div>"},{"n":48,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The area inside the parabola 5x<sup>2</sup> – y = 0 but outside parabola 2x<sup>2</sup> – y + 9 = 0 is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f2/f2299b3412d059f5a0c4.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d4/d4f65612ab61969f1af8.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ab/ab51ce7c7ac7cfd5f653.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f0/f083fc33b51204113b24.png\" />"}],"answer":["A"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(a)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e5/e5d373f814a1bcd4070a.png\" /></div>"},{"n":49,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A city of population 8 lakh generates municipal solid waste (MSW) at a rate of 0.5 kg per capita per day. About 40% of the total waste is recycled, and the remaining waste is disposed off in a landfill. The compacted density of MSW in the landfill is 500 kg/m<sup>3</sup> and the landfill has a maximum height of 12 m (neglecting cover and side slopes). The plan area of the landfill required for 10<br />\nyears of operation is _____ ha. (Answer upto one decimal place).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[14.4,14.8],"answerText":"14.6","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>14.6 (14.4 - 14.8)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/83/835cca0a8f36a1239ce5.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":50,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The basic runway length is 1650 m. After application of all corrections. Basic runway length increased by 40%, Airport reference temperature is 20°C more than standard atmospheric tamperature. The effective gradient of runway is 0.5%.<br />\nThe elevation of airport is ______ m. (Correct upto two decimal places)</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[259,260.25],"answerText":"259.74","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>259.74 (259 - 260.25)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/44/443be25abe66cc54ddb2.png\" /></div>"},{"n":51,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>The ambient air contains carbon monoxide at a concentration of 6 mg/m<sup>3</sup> measured at a temperature of 30°C and a pressure of 0.98 atm. Considering ideal gas law valid, the equivalent concentration of CO in ppm at STP is _____ ppm. (Answer upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[5.2,5.7],"answerText":"5.44","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>5.44 (5.20 - 5.70)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6f/6fe019bd3570eadf732b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":52,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A valley curve of length 250 m is to be formed where a descending gradient of 1 in 25 meets an ascending gradient of 1 in 40. The distance of the lowest point on the valley curve from initial tangent point is ______ m (Correct upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[138,139],"answerText":"138.68","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>138.68 (138 - 139)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/78/788e327fdfdfec6db521.png\" /></div>"},{"n":53,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>In a triangle, the observed angles are:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6c/6c57c0b523e0ba56ea0b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>The value and weight of angle <em>C</em>, respectively, are:</div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"75°59'20''; 0.83"},{"key":"B","html":"75°59'40''; 0.83"},{"key":"C","html":"75°59'20''; 0.20"},{"key":"D","html":"75°59'20''; 1.20"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a5/a57d5cdbd68113087f47.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":54,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The moment of <em>A</em> for the frame shown in figure below is:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/f3/f33bbfdac55a347b4067.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"12 kN-m"},{"key":"B","html":"6 kN-m"},{"key":"C","html":"8 kN-m"},{"key":"D","html":"4 kN-m"}],"answer":["C"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"C","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/66/6656f707c201178dce3e.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6e/6e161ff773551f1fe636.png\" /></div>"},{"n":55,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A wall footing which is 2 m wide at the base at 1.5 m below ground level is resting in cohesive soil. The clay soil has γ = 20 kN/m<sup>3</sup>, C = 40 kN/m<sup>2</sup>, <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/96/96555fcde32fe29dae25.png\" /> = 25°. Now by assuming the soil as soft and likely to fail under local shear, the safe bearing capacity of soil per meter length of the footing is:<br />\n[Take FOS = 2.5]</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/fe/fe0770ec23164b862511.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"548.00 kN/m"},{"key":"B","html":"450.00 kN/m"},{"key":"C","html":"246.816 kN/m"},{"key":"D","html":"493.64 kN/m"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3f/3fe9ed36234a21889ca0.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a4/a49c115774d342c1f323.png\" /></div>"},{"n":56,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>On a particular day total 130 m<sup>3</sup> of concrete is casted for RCC work. A total of 6 cubes are to be casted for one sample for 7 day and 28 days testing of concrete.<br />\nIn the present case how many number of samples will be required for testing of concrete for compressive strength test as per IS 456: 2000 ________ (in integers)?</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[6,6],"answerText":"6","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>6 (6 - 6)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/77/777a7288544abe4b213b.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":57,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0","html":"<p>A cylindrical soil specimen of diameter 80 mm and height 160 mm weighs 1.90 kg along with container in its natural state. The porosity of the specimen is 38%. The specific gravity of solids is 2.65. The specimen is then fully saturated by adding water and its weight increases by 0.06 kg. The air content of the soil in its natural state is _____ %. (Answer upto two decimal places).</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[19.3,20],"answerText":"19.63","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>19.63 (19.30 - 20.0)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6c/6ca6700d1808e0eb5dab.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ae/ae147cd14ff8644ea18f.png\" /></div>"},{"n":58,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>The corner of an existing building is 10 m from centre line on a curved portion of two-lane highway, the radius of curve being 160 m. Considering the stopping sight distance criterion, the safe operating speed if the radius of curve measured from centerline of road is ________ kmph (correct upto two decimal places).<br />\nAssume reaction time of driver as 2.5 sec, longitudinal friction coefficient as 0.40, lane width is 3.5 m and length of curve is greater than stopping sight distance.</p>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[72,73.5],"answerText":"72.79","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>72.79 (72 - 73.5)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/cc/cc9a03df896dc85929f5.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/0d/0d9cf55ad985b6c04690.png\" /></div>"},{"n":59,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A steel beam has a T-shaped cross-section as shown in the figure. If the beam is subjected to a vertical shear force of 120 kN at the section, then the maximum shear stress in the web at this section is ___ MPa. (Answer upto two decimal places).</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/49/49ec6613d3fe045ba5b3.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[16.7,17.2],"answerText":"16.92","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>16.92 (16.70 - 17.20)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d1/d1d6a4567635178e48f8.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/3b/3b3aaac8049b1785d107.png\" /></div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"},{"n":60,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>A rolled I-section beam is supported on a 100 mm wide bearing plate as shown in the figure. The thickness of flange and web of the I-section are 11.5 mm and 7.5 mm respectively. Radius at root of the I-section is 16.5 mm. As per IS 800 : 2007, the web bearing strength of the beam will be<br />\nTake: f<em><sub>y</sub></em> = 250 MPa and γ<em><sub>mo</sub></em> = 1.1</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/6b/6b1c4a11ca1257bbfe2f.png\" /></div>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"200.74 kN"},{"key":"B","html":"250.78 kN"},{"key":"C","html":"210.67 kN"},{"key":"D","html":"289.77 kN"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/34/34c97d78249183044faf.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":61,"type":"NAT","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A section of a gravity dam built of concrete is shown in the figure:</p>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/09/09d6a281e5a89be7cf43.png\" /></div>\n\n<div> </div>\n\n<div>If the eccentricity e for the dam section with loads acting as such is 5.6 m (towards toe), then the maximum vertical stress acting at toe is _______ kN/m<sup>2</sup>. (Answer upto one decimal place).</div>","options":[],"answer":null,"natRange":[567.5,568.5],"answerText":"567.9","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>567.9 (567.5 - 568.5)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8d/8df396942b767a2a3baf.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/63/6378ea8a8a240e219dbe.png\" /></div>"},{"n":62,"type":"MSQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0","html":"<p>A rectangular primary sedimentation tank of size 20 m × 8 m × 3.2 m receives water from a town having a population of 25000 with a per capita water supply of 120 l/day. The maximum daily flow is 1.8 times the average daily flow. The influent suspended solids concentration is 80 mg/l and the tank removes 65% of the suspended solids. The specific gravity of the deposited solids is<br />\n2.5. Based on the above data, which of the following statements is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"The detention time in the tank is 2.276 hours."},{"key":"B","html":"The horizontal flow velocity in the tank is 2.441 mm/sec."},{"key":"C","html":"The rate of dry solids deposited is 432 kg/day."},{"key":"D","html":"The overflow rate of the tank is 96.43 m<sup>3</sup>/day/m<sup>2</sup>."}],"answer":["A","B"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"A, B","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0},"solution":"<p>(a, b)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/08/08a9099612702c2d6dfa.png\" /></div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>"},{"n":63,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>If integrating factor of the differential equation <img align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\" src=\"media/2e/2efaa224ec5c0a375625.png\" /> then <em>P</em> is equal to</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e0/e0a388942969d35c025f.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/dd/ddef3727a2cb63151e30.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/30/302e83c90af4289c0c59.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/8e/8e730210d1d24de50170.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/4f/4fb01ecc19bce8c43845.png\" /></div>"},{"n":64,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +2 / -0.66","html":"<p>The angle between the surfaces x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> + z<sup>2</sup> = 9 and z = x<sup>2</sup> + y<sup>2</sup> – 3 at the point (2, –1, 2) is</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/e1/e16a783f86993b95631c.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/75/757c4be45d910649890e.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/d9/d9f43cedf40df08a6c80.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<div> </div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/25/25cf6c6e9c0a9e356e86.png\" /></div>"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":2,"neg":0.66},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/a0/a0facd8e6f3fde3bf10d.png\" /></div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/7f/7fd4d6a52160dfbdfdec.png\" /></div>"},{"n":65,"type":"MCQ","section":"Technical","tags":"Technical • CIVIL ENGINEERING • +1 / -0.33","html":"<p>The equation <em>x</em><sup>3</sup> – <em>x</em><sup>2</sup> + 4<em>x</em> – 4 = 0 is to be solved using the Newton-Raphson method. If <em>x</em> = 2 is taken as the initial approximation of the solution, then the first approximation using this method will be</p>","options":[{"key":"A","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/29/2912b37f1e4a0c370c88.png\" />"},{"key":"B","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/92/92a115be7a425f49761d.png\" />"},{"key":"C","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/ab/ab2876ad6a5228a70089.png\" />"},{"key":"D","html":"<img alt=\"\" src=\"media/04/044c6e5cea2111871058.png\" />"}],"answer":["D"],"natRange":null,"answerText":"D","marks":{"pos":1,"neg":0.33},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div><img alt=\"\" src=\"media/c5/c577d1b5c4b02c8b9a1f.png\" /></div>"}],"math":false,"scoring":"marks","sections":[{"name":"General Aptitude","start":0,"count":10},{"name":"Technical","start":10,"count":55}],"stats":{"questions":65,"maxMarks":100,"types":{"MCQ":35,"NAT":26,"MSQ":4},"withoutKey":0}};
